  <p>
    An MOT test centre rarely runs MOT testing in isolation — retests, advisories that turn into repair work, and
    general servicing all sit alongside the test slots. GarageCloud puts MOT bookings on the same workshop board as
    everything else, so a failed test with repair work booked in doesn't need a second system to track.
  </p>

  <h2>What an MOT test centre needs day to day</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Test slots scheduled on the same board as repair and service bookings.</li>
    <li>MOT reminders sent automatically ahead of each vehicle's due date.</li>
    <li>VRM lookup to confirm vehicle details before the test starts.</li>
    <li>A straight path from a failed advisory to a booked repair, without re-entering the vehicle.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Retests and repairs, tracked together</h2>
  <p>
    When a test results in advisories or a fail, the natural next step is booking the repair. Keeping that on the
    same system as the test itself — rather than a standalone MOT tool — means the retest gets booked against a job
    that already has the vehicle's full inspection detail attached.
  </p>
